  "language": "en",
  "question": {
    "prompt": "Given \\(A=x^2+2x\\) and \\(B=2x^2-x+3\\), simplifying \\(2A-B\\) gives \\(ax+b\\), where \\(a\\) and \\(b\\) are constants. Find the value of \\(a+b\\)."
  },
  "schemaVersion": "3.0",
  "solutions": [
    {
      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_035",
        "cnm_034"
      ],
      "explanation": "\\(2A-B=2x^2+4x-2x^2+x-3=5x-3\\), so \\(a=5\\), \\(b=-3\\), and \\(a+b=2\\).",
